SUMMARY:Intermediate Spanish Book Club
DESCRIPTION:Join us at our new Intermediate Spanish Book Club! We offer a 
 welcoming space for readers at the A2/B1 Spanish level who want to improve 
 their language skills through engaging literature and conversation. Our 
 first book will be "Cajas de Cartón" by Francisco Jiménez. We will 
 explore this powerful autobiographical collection of stories while 
 practicing our Spanish reading and discussion skills. We will be discussing 
 the first 4 chapters of the book at the first meeting. \n\nWho Should 
 Join?\n\n· Learners reading at an A2-B1 level.\n\n· Adults interested in 
 improving Spanish through literature.\n\n· Anyone who enjoys thoughtful 
 discussion in a supportive environment.\n\nRegistration is required. Please 
 register for each meeting you plan to attend\n\nQuestions? Please contact 
 Jessica at jllundin@dconc.gov or group facilitator Renee Carroll at 
 renecarol33@gmail.com\n
LOCATION:Adult Programming Room\, South Regional Library (4505 S. Alston Ave)
ORGANIZER;CN="Jessica L.":MAILTO:jllundin@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Book Club, Spanish
UID:LibCal-14288-16712016
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/16712016
