BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260527T220000Z
DTEND:20260527T233000Z
DTSTAMP:20260527T000000Z
SUMMARY:Networking for Introverts: Unleashing Your SUPERPOWER
DESCRIPTION:If the idea of a "mixer" makes you want to find that quiet 
 corner seat next to the snacks and stay there\, welcome home. Most 
 networking advice uses a one-size-fits-all approach that doesn't always 
 account for how we're wired.\n\nThis is for the rest of us—the 
 observers\, the listeners\, and those who notice the small details others 
 might miss. We aren’t here to change who you are\; we’re here to help 
 you activate your natural traits and turn them into your greatest 
 professional asset. \n\nWho Should Be There:\n\n\n	Early in your career: 
 Learn the "cheat codes" to networking before you burn out trying to play a 
 character that isn't you.\n	The "Curious" (Nosey) Extroverts: We see you. 
 Come see how we navigate the world \n	The Workforce Folks: You want to find 
 real talent? Stop looking at the loudest person and start looking at the 
 one who’s actually processing the data.\n\n\nThe "Business Whisperer" 
 Reality Check: We’re going deep into the science of why our brains work 
 differently. It’s not "shyness"—it’s Business Intelligence.\n\n⚠️ 
 SPOILER ALERT: This is a live session. We’re doing 
 Intro’speriments.\n\n\n	Pro-Tip: Show up early. Scout your seat. Get 
 settled. We’re going to practice networking in a way that doesn’t drain 
 you.\n\n\n \n\n \n\nJacinta Walker's Bio: The Business Whisperer\n\nI’m a 
 professional growth architect and strategic consultant with 25 years of 
 experience mastering the "Invisible Edge." People call me the Business 
 Whisperer and the Networking Queen\, which is a bit of a paradox: I’m a 
 high-functioning introvert who can work a room better than most 
 extroverts.\n\nThe Secret? I’m not playing a character—I’m activating 
 my observation skills. While everyone else focuses on the noise\, I listen 
 for what isn't being said.\n\nWhy No One Believes I’m an Introvert: If 
 you’ve seen me on stage at 1 Million Cups or leading a session at the 
 Durham Tech\, you’d think I was born for the spotlight. But I’ll be the 
 first to tell you that after a day of "Real Talking\," my only goal is a 
 nap to recharge. I don’t see introversion as a barrier\; I see it as a 
 SUPERPOWER for deep connection and strategic business intelligence.\n\n\n\n
LOCATION:Conference Room #3214\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Ciera Williams":MAILTO:cbwilliams@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Business, Career Development
UID:LibCal-14288-16861353
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/16861353
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260527T220000Z
DTEND:20260527T233000Z
DTSTAMP:20260527T000000Z
SUMMARY:Romance Lovers Book Club-The Emperor and the Endless Palace and Butterfly Swords
DESCRIPTION:All things romance!\n\nThis book club talks about all things 
 romance\, starting with the month's theme but quickly branching out into 
 other books we've been reading and loving\, books we want to read\, and 
 what's going on in Romancelandia - you'll walk away every month with lots 
 of recs for your TBR! Because of our wide-ranging discussions\, you should 
 always feel free to drop in even if you haven't gotten a chance to try the 
 book club picks. This month we're reading\, The Emperor and the Endless 
 Palace by Justinian Huang and Butterfly Swords by Jeannie Lin. If you want 
 to attend this virtual event\, please register or contact Chelsea Romero at 
 cromero@dconc.gov with any questions.
LOCATION:North Regional Library (221 Milton Rd)
ORGANIZER;CN="Chelsea Romero":MAILTO:cromero@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Book Club
UID:LibCal-14288-16416418
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/16416418
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260527T220000Z
DTEND:20260527T233000Z
DTSTAMP:20260527T000000Z
SUMMARY:Wednesday Computer Class @ Main
DESCRIPTION:Come join a supportive group environment for self-paced digital 
 skills courses. We'll be using Northstar Digital Literacy\, a free online 
 resource available to all Durham County Library patrons. A library staff 
 member will be present to get you set up and answer questions as each 
 participant moves through online modules on their own at their own pace. 
 Northstar allows you to track your learning progress and earn badges or 
 certificates for completing a course. These classes are best for learners 
 who have at least basic keyboard and mouse skills. Our computer lab has a 
 limited number of laptops for use\, so bringing your own laptop and 
 headphones is encouraged.\n\nComputer and digital skills topics 
 include:\n\n\n	Phone Keyboard Basics & Logging In\n	Basic Computer 
 Skills\n	Internet Basics\n	Using Email\n	Windows 10 & 11\n	Mac 
 OS\n	Microsoft Word\, Excel\, and PowerPoint\n	Google Docs\n	Social 
 Media\n	Information Literacy\n	Career Search Skills\n	Your Digital 
 Footprint\n	Accessing Telehealth Appointments\n	Cybersecurity 
 Basics\n\n\nThese classes are self-paced and each week participants will 
 choose which lessons they want to complete on their own. You do not need to 
 have come to the first class to attend the following weeks and there is no 
 requirement to commit to all of the classes through June. Register for the 
 weeks that work best for you!\n\nIf you have any questions or accommodation 
 needs\, contact Jimmy McKinnell at jmckinnell@dconc.gov or call 
 919-560-9940\n\n\nÚnase a un ambiente de apoyo para cursos de habilidades 
 digitales a su propio ritmo. Usaremos Northstar Digital Literacy\, un 
 recurso en línea gratuito que también está disponible en español para 
 todos los usuarios de la Biblioteca del Condado de Durham. Un miembro del 
 personal de la biblioteca estará presente para ayudarle a comenzar y 
 responder sus preguntas mientras cada participante avanza por los módulos 
 en línea de manera individual y a su propio ritmo. Northstar le permite 
 llevar un registro de su progreso y obtener insignias o certificados al 
 completar un curso. Estas clases son ideales para personas que ya cuentan 
 con habilidades básicas de teclado y mouse. Nuestro laboratorio de 
 computación tiene una cantidad limitada de laptops disponibles\, por lo 
 que se recomienda traer su propio laptop y audífonos.\n\nLos temas de 
 computación y habilidades digitales incluyen:\n\n\n	Conceptos básicos del 
 teclado del teléfono e inicio de sesión\n	Habilidades básicas de 
 computación\n	Conceptos básicos de Internet\n	Uso del correo 
 electrónico\n	Windows 10 & 11\n	Mac OS\n	Microsoft Word\, Excel y 
 PowerPoint\n	Google Docs\n	Redes sociales\n	Alfabetización 
 informacional\n	Habilidades para la búsqueda de empleo\n	Su huella 
 digital\n	Cómo acceder a citas de telesalud\n	Conceptos básicos de 
 ciberseguridad\n\n\nEstas clases son autodirigidas y cada semana los 
 participantes elegirán qué lecciones desean completar por su cuenta. No 
 necesita haber asistido a la primera clase para participar en las 
 siguientes sesiones\, y no es necesario comprometerse a todas las clases 
 hasta junio. ¡Inscríbase en las semanas que mejor le funcionen!\n\nSi 
 tiene preguntas o necesita alguna adaptación\, comuníquese con Jimmy 
 McKinnell a jmckinnell@dconc.gov o llame al 919-560-9940.\n
LOCATION:Computer Lab\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="James McKinnell":MAILTO:jmckinnell@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Computer Class, Digital/Tech Literacy
UID:LibCal-14288-16677662
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/16677662
END:VEVENT
