SUMMARY:Garden Club for Kids @ Southwest
DESCRIPTION:Do you love gardening\, nature\, and being outside? Children 
 ages 7-12 are invited to join Southwest's Garden Club. Once a month\, we'll 
 get together in Southwest's backyard garden to talk about gardening\, plant 
 things\, and work on garden tasks. Once we get into mid-summer\, we'll also 
 begin harvesting vegetables and herbs to taste and share. Seeds & seedlings 
 will be available for participants to take home. \n\nThis month\, garlic 
 will be ready to harvest! \n\nThis program is geared towards children ages 
 7 \, but caregivers are welcome to join us as well. Registration is 
 required. This is an outdoor program\, so please be sure to dress in 
 comfortable clothing and bring water & sunscreen. In the event of rain\, 
 this program will be canceled. If you have any questions\, please email 
 Kristen at kstockdale@dconc.gov. \n\nLet's grow together!
LOCATION:Southwest Regional - Children's Programming Room\, Southwest Regional Library (3605 Shannon Rd)
ORGANIZER;CN="Kristen Stockdale":MAILTO:kstockdale@dconc.gov
