SUMMARY:All Things STEAM: Let's Learn About Fireflies!
DESCRIPTION:To all youths ages 7-11 years and their caregivers: join Ms. 
 Natalie to explore STEAM (Science\, Technology\, Engineering\, Art\, and 
 Mathematics)! Every first Thursday of the month\, we will discuss a 
 different STEAM topic and further our learning with a hands-on activity or 
 craft.\n\nIn celebration of the beginning of the summer\, we will learn 
 about fireflies' bioluminescence and create our own glowing fireflies using 
 batteries\, copper tape\, LED lights\, and other materials! You may see 
 some real fireflies outside\, if you try looking for them!\n\nRegistration 
 is required.\n\nIf you have any questions\, please contact us @ 
 919-560-8592.
LOCATION:Southwest Regional - Children's Programming Room\, Southwest Regional Library (3605 Shannon Rd)
ORGANIZER;CN="Natalie Perez":MAILTO:natperez@dconc.gov
