SUMMARY:Open Office Hours: Small Business Assistance from SCORE
DESCRIPTION:Have the beginnings of a business idea? Need some assistance 
 figuring out a path to entrepreneurship? Looking for support to grow your 
 business? SCORE can help you start\, grow or successfully exit a 
 business.\n\nFrom diverse backgrounds and industries\, SCORE mentors know 
 what it’s like to be a small business owner.  Partnering with 
 entrepreneurs one-on-one\, SCORE mentors support small business success by 
 providing experienced advice\, consulting on best practices\, and education 
 on business topics. Anyone can successfully start a business with the right 
 support--connect with a mentor and get the guidance you need to grow and 
 thrive. Small business owners who receive three or more hours of mentoring 
 report higher revenues and increased growth. \n\nThis program is "open 
 office hours" style--first come\, first served--every Tuesday (12-4) & 
 Thursday (1-4). Mentors will be here to help you on your entrepreneurial 
 journey! \n\nRegister at the 4th floor information desk. \n\n \n\nWe also 
 host SCORE's Welcome to Entrepreneurship\, Understanding How to Price Your 
 Product or Service and Introduction to Recordkeeping workshops!\n\n \n\n 
 \n\n \n\n \n\n \n\n
LOCATION:Main Study Room #4304\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Jana Bradley":MAILTO:jbradley@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Business, Career Development
UID:LibCal-14288-16046147
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/16046147
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260609T170000Z
DTEND:20260609T210000Z
DTSTAMP:20260609T000000Z
SUMMARY:This Week In the Lab: Paper Crafts
DESCRIPTION:Join the STEAM Team in the Innovation Lab during specified open 
 hours to do paper crafts by creating your own Zine and fold 
 origami!\n\nZines (pronounced "zeens") are tough to define because they can 
 be so many things! Basically\, they are self-published\nbooklets containing 
 anything you want - art\, writing\, drawings\, recipes\, poetry\, comics\, 
 etc. The content and look\nare totally up to the creator. It's all about 
 self-expression. Origami is an ancient art technique to fold paper into 
 exciting and unexpected shapes.\n\nThis is a self-paced activity. You can 
 drop in during the listed Open Lab Hours.\n\nInnovation Lab Open 
 Hours:\n\nMonday: Closed\nTuesday: 1pm - 5pm\nWednesday: 3pm - 
 7pm\nThursday: 10am - 2pm\nFriday: 1pm - 5pm\nSaturday: 3pm - 5pm 
 (*different this week)\n\nHours subject to change based on staffing and 
 programming needs.
