SUMMARY:DIY Needle Felted Dinosaur Sculptures for Tweens & Teens
DESCRIPTION:Participants ages 9  will learn the basics of needle felting 
 and walk away with their own woolly creation. No experience needed\, just a 
 willingness to stab some fluff with a sharp needle and see what happens. 
 During this 2-hour program\, we'll create fluffy dinosaurs! \n\nWhat is 
 needle felting? Think of it like sculpture\, but instead of clay you've got 
 fluffy colorful wool and a pokey needle. No mess\, no glue\, just stab 
 until something awesome appears.\n\nThis program is geared towards children 
 ages 9  - please note that we will be using sharp needles to complete this 
 project. Caregivers are welcome to join and participate if they'd like. 
 \n\nDue to limited supplies\, registration is required. Questions? Please 
 reach out to Ms. Kristen at kstockdale@dconc.gov
LOCATION:Southwest Regional - Children's Programming Room\, Southwest Regional Library (3605 Shannon Rd)
ORGANIZER;CN="Kristen Stockdale":MAILTO:kstockdale@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Arts & Crafts, Maker, Sensory Friendly, Summer Reading
