BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260612T200000Z
DTEND:20260612T213000Z
DTSTAMP:20260612T000000Z
SUMMARY:Durham Refugee Day Film Screening
DESCRIPTION:\n\nCelebrate Durham Refugee Day with a Month of Powerful Film 
 Screenings!\n\nThis June\, we are honored to recognize Durham Refugee Day 
 with three special community film screenings. Each event is crafted to 
 uplift the journeys\, voices\, and contributions of our newest neighbors. 
 Through these films\, attendees will gain meaningful insight into why 
 families leave their home countries\, how they rebuild their lives here in 
 Durham\, and the traditions\, skills\, and strengths they bring to our 
 shared community.\n\nEach screening will feature a curated block of short 
 films that highlight stories of resilience and reflect the lived 
 experiences of refugees around the world. Screenings will be hosted at both 
 the Durham County Main Library and Russell Memorial CME Church.\n\nWhether 
 you’re newly exploring these conversations or already engaged in refugee 
 support efforts\, we warmly invite you to join us. Come watch\, reflect\, 
 and learn together as we honor the diverse stories that continue to shape 
 the fabric of Durham.\n\nWe look forward to seeing you there!\n\n
LOCATION:Main Auditorium\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Maria Ramirez-Heuser":MAILTO:mrheuser@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Community Engagement, Durham, Low Sensory Stimulation, Movie, Social
UID:LibCal-14288-16768303
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/16768303
END:VEVENT
